            <ArticleTitle>Opiate receptor binding and behavioral effects of morphine in RHA/Verh and RLA/Verh rats.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>485-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Large baseline differences were found in open field activity and rearing behavior between 2 psychogenetically selected rat lines, as well as differences in the effects of peripherally administered morphine (2,4 and 10 mg/kg) on those behaviors and on body temperature. The 2 lines also showed different capacities of tritiated DAGO binding to preparations of striatal membranes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
